# Amendment cycle — pyyaml-reachability amendment (#5, 2026-04-22,
# fifth amendment): amendment #4 unblocked the detachment + partial-
# recovery path but left end-to-end S4 failing on fresh clones. The
# detached worker's Phase-4a scaffold invocation imported workspace_
# bootstrap.adapters.first_run_scaffold in-process under the system
# Python 3.13 interpreter that first-run.sh detected on PATH. The
# workspace_bootstrap package transitively loads yaml (pyyaml) via
# manifest.py, pydantic via spec.py, and opentelemetry via host.py —
# all three live only in the shared venv installed in Phase 3b; the
# system interpreter had none. The worker crashed with
# ``ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yaml'`` before the scaffold
# ever ran. Amendment #5 invokes the scaffold as a subprocess under
# the shared venv's Python via a new thin CLI runner
# (hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_scaffold_runner.py). The
# runner's top imports are stdlib-only; the adapter import happens
# inside main() after argv parse. Exit code + stderr JSON protocol
# preserves the adapter's exception class in the surfaced diagnostic.
